Unicode data
------------

    src/lib/unicode13.js   the code points Unicode 13.0 assigns
    src/lib/codecs.js      in part: SINGLE_BYTE_CODECS, the characters
                           each single-byte codec decodes bytes to

These tables are read from Python 3.10's unicodedata and from Python's
codecs, whose single-byte codecs CPython made for the most part from the
Unicode Consortium's mapping tables. They are Unicode data, distributed under
the Unicode License v3 (LICENSE-UNICODE; SPDX: Unicode-3.0):

    Copyright © 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc.


Codec names
-----------

src/lib/codecs.js also lists, in PY_CODEC_ALIASES, the names Python's codecs
answer to, read from Python by scripts/make_codec_tables.py so that a coding
cookie is read as Python reads it. They are facts about Python, not its code.
